Z||000000||gtsonly||09-11-2000||09:09 AM||||I am looking to install a 1995 Pontiac Trans Am AC Delco stereo into my 86 Fiero. What do I need if anything to complete this job? I have heard that the wiring harness is different and you need to buy an adapter. One more question about Theftlock. The dealership wants to charge me 30 bucks to reset the Factory Theftlock codes. Is there a way to do that yourself? Can you get the codes from the internet? Anyone ever deal with this before? Thanks for the help!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPS<BR>http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/ubbmisc.cgi||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfixit58||09-11-2000||10:06 AM||||You need to talk to these guys:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.newellelectronics.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.newellelectronics.com/</A> <P>He has an adapter that costs approx $20. Good people to deal with. Also, look under the topic "Locked Radio" for instructions on obtaining the secondary code. You will need this code for the dealership to give you the operation code. Newell may also be able to help you once you have the secondary code. <P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||lou_dias||09-11-2000||10:38 PM||||You can buy an adapter at Circuit City for under $15.  I have a 98 Blazer CD Player deck in my GT.  An upgrade in speakers will be required as that sucker will blow the stock speakers if the volume goes past half way to the max.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RossT||09-12-2000||02:41 AM||||GM has the part= 16140051  includes everything you need.||||reg||1
